WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.846
Start with the question: how do we answer from a document collection without inventing missing information?

2
00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:27.692
The application connects a FastAPI backend with a browser chat interface.

3
00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:41.538
Ingestion splits documents into sentence-aware chunks instead of arbitrary character slices.

4
00:00:41.538 --> 00:00:55.384
The default feature-hashing embedder works without downloading a model.

5
00:00:55.384 --> 00:01:09.230
A cosine vector store finds candidates. Re-ranking blends similarity with keyword overlap.

6
00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:23.076
The extractive reader answers from retrieved context and abstains when the context is insufficient.

7
00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:36.923
Source citations connect the answer to its originating chunk.

8
00:01:36.923 --> 00:01:50.769
A router sends arithmetic questions to a restricted AST calculator and other questions to RAG.

9
00:01:50.769 --> 00:02:04.615
Server-Sent Events stream responses through the chat endpoint.

10
00:02:04.615 --> 00:02:18.461
The evaluation harness checks retrieval hit-rate, reciprocal rank, faithfulness and answer relevance.

11
00:02:18.461 --> 00:02:32.307
Configuration can swap in sentence-transformers, pgvector, Ollama, Gemini or OpenAI backends.

12
00:02:32.307 --> 00:02:46.153
The limitation: sample-corpus checks do not establish reliability across arbitrary documents.

13
00:02:46.153 --> 00:03:00.000
Explore the backend, tests and evaluation code. The best evidence is the implementation itself.

